    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog focuses heavily on exploiting favorable park factors and SP matchups against sub-5.00 xERA arms to squeeze value out of our OF unit. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) is our unequivocal strongest play of the day; he draws a prime matchup against Zack Littell, and the combination of an elite park factor (+10%) and a significant platoon edge (+13%) makes him a foundational piece. We also see high-ceiling production from **Gavin Sheets** (62.32), who benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Dobnak, and **Dylan Beavers** (61.84), whose platoon advantage against Arrighetti keeps his efficiency well above our 60-point threshold for a strong start. While **Bryce Harper** (59.49) faces a tougher arm in Manaea, his elite xwOBA of 0.391 ensures he remains a must-start in the UTIL slot despite the marginal platoon penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.06). While he possesses the requisite speed to impact our scarcest category, his efficiency score was dragged down by an unfavorable matchup against Bryan Woo and the inherent risk of the lineup remaining pending. The optimizer ultimately favored **Geraldo Perdomo** (56.17) for the MI slot, prioritizing the 8% order boost associated with his #2 spot, which provides a more stable floor than **Jung Hoo Lee** could offer in the #6 hole. Elsewhere, **Cal Raleigh** (54.30) and **Luis Arraez** (50.37) are starts we are monitoring closely; both are listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" and should their confirmed spots drop lower in the order, their daily efficiency could dip toward our \"Marginal\" threshold. We have opted to bench **Ryan Waldschmidt** (45.19) and **Drew Gilbert** (38.71) today, as their current projected output does not justify taking the cap hit over our higher-scoring OF and MI depth.",
